      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TAIPAN TOMMY (4) is a tough veteran with a terrific record here over the trip. He is peaking at the right time, and with a drop in class, he should go close to taking this out, especially with the aid of the pole position. STARTON (2) is a very consistent gelding who has made a bright start to this season with a brace of second place finishes. He has yet to win over this trip, but has placed in 9 of his 11 starts, so stick with him for all top 4 combos. COURS VITE (5) is getting closer to breaking his course duck after a string of minor placings this season. She only needs a genuine tempo up top for her to produce her customary big finish. Each way. VALLEY PRINCE (8) resumes from a short break that would have done him no harm. His record says it all, and he is always a top 4 player whenever he lines up on this home track. OKESUTORA (1) found the front without too much trouble last start, and that was the key to him winning. Stick with him in the same class.",
